From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:55:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] PeripheralCecAdapter: bring the amp to the level shown

A CEC amp reports its level only when asked, and a request and its
answer take ~150 ms of a bus the keys also need. It does not acknowledge
a key for a moment after acting on one, acknowledges but ignores a key
that follows the last one within ~300 ms, and answers with the level and
mute state from before the keys it has not acted on yet. The level shown
lagged the keys, ran ahead of the amp, or was put back by a late answer,
and a release that was not acknowledged was not sent again, which leaves
the key held on the amp. It takes a press repeated within ~300 ms for a
held key and moves on its own, much faster than taps, by an amount the
keys do not tell. An amp on CEC 1.4 has no <Set Audio Volume Level> to
set a level outright.

Once the amp has reported a level, let the volume keys set the level
wanted and show it as the key is pressed: one step a press, one every
100 ms while a key is held. The first key after a 3 s pause counts from
the level the amp reports then, whatever set it, read before the amp is
moved. The adapter thread brings the amp to the level wanted as fast as
it goes: more than 4 steps away, the key is held on the amp and the amp
is read all along, released 4 steps short; once a level read 300 ms
after the release is in, the rest is tapped, each tap a press and a
release 600 ms apart, counting only the taps the amp acknowledged and
sending again 50 ms later any key it did not, a single press up to four
times, a release until it is acknowledged, to the device the key was
pressed on. A device that acknowledges no key for 2 s is given up on. A
key queued before the amp reported a level moves the level shown with it
once the level is known. Some inputs repeat a held key without a hold
time: the same action within 100 ms of the last one is taken for a
repeat, and a mute repeated that way is dropped like a held one. Keys
pressed while CEC is disabled are not sent once it is enabled again.

1 s after the last key, ask the amp for its level and mute state, and
ignore any answer before that; it is not asked while it is being brought
to the level, nor while a key is held. Bring the amp to the level shown
wherever it settled, until it settles no closer twice in a row (the
amp's second answer to a request does not count), as at a limit set on
the amp; show the amp's level then, and whenever it is reported other
than after volume keys. An answer with no level (0x7F) still carries the
mute state. An amp can take more than a second to report a mute: until 3
s after a mute key is pressed or taken, an answer at odds with the mute
state it set is asked again 500 ms later, unless a volume key, which can
unmute the amp, followed. When a key is dropped unsent, flip the mute
state flipped with it back, and ask the amp for the one it kept. The
volume bar opened while muted stays open until the next volume action,
so give it one when the amp turns out not to be muted after all, a mute
key that opened it is dropped, or the amp no longer handles volume. Wait
150 ms after an answer before asking again: an amp can answer a request
twice, ~110 ms apart.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
